From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <jameswdumay@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 20:05:00 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(skippy): key shared-KV state effects on owner cache layer

Gemma3n/Gemma4 reuse an earlier layer's KV cache for layers at or beyond
n_layer_kv_from_start. Consumer layers read the owner's storage through
map_layer_ids while the state effect records the access-site layer, so
stage program admission sees two (kind, layer) bindings on one storage
root and rejects the program ("state root has conflicting semantics").

Record a storage-identity layer on each state effect: the owner cache
layer for shared-KV readers, else the access-site layer. Admission and
the state roots key on that identity; residency and write ordinals keep
the access-site layer. Consumers never write shared KV, so ordinals are
unchanged.
